|> Exercise
    handle=_dimensional_cos_f_
    For which signatures of $k : \rr \ra \rr$ are
    $$
    \Large \cos \circ\,k
    $$
    and
    $$
    \Large k \circ \cos
    $$
    and 
    $$
    \Large \cos \circ\, k \circ k
    $$
    and 
    $$
    \Large k \circ k \circ \cos
    $$
    and 
    $$
    \Large k \circ \cos \circ\, k
    $$
    and, lastly,
    $$
    \Large \cos \circ\, k \circ \cos
    $$
    well-formed compositions? (Separately for
    each.)

    |> Solution

        Because

        $$
        \cos : [1] \ra [1]
        $$

        inputs and outputs dimensionless values,

        $$
        \cos \circ\, k
        $$

        requires a $k$ of the form

        $$
        k : [\tA] \ra [1]
        $$

        for some arbitrary units A,
        so that the output of $k$ can be fed to $\cos$,
        while

        $$
        k \circ \cos
        $$

        requires a $k$ of the form

        $$
        k : [1] \ra [\tA]
        $$

        so that the output of $\cos$ is compatible with $k$.

        All of the other combinations require

        $$
        k : [1] \ra [1]
        $$

        since they either involve

        $$
        k \circ k
        $$

        that requires $k$ of the form $k : [A] \ra [A]$,
        but “touching” $\cos$ at one end further forcing $[A] = [1]$,
        or else both of the combinations
        “$k \circ \cos$” and “$\cos \circ\, k$” in the same expression,
        !! involve $k$ both accepting inputs from $\cos$
        !! and passing outputs on to $\cos$, 
        directly forcing the input
        and output units of $k$ to be dimensionless.
